## Ten more themes are kept in parked_themes.gd; to use one again, move it back into THEMES.
##
## Word themes. Every time a recipe book is opened the frog (ThemeFrog) picks its theme, and only
## that theme's words are used in it. Each word is in exactly one theme.
## A theme needs at least 20 words that fit each book, so it can be brewed twice without a repeat
## (the smoke test checks this); extra words give variety.
## Entry: [word, meaning (must not give the word away), pictures].
## Pictures: emoji with spaces between them, the most telling one first. "@mole" = the drawing
## art/pictures/mole.svg, for things no emoji shows well. A word needs as many as the most
## letters that can be missing from it (1 for 3 letters ... 5 for 9 or more); the smoke test checks this.
## Levels pick words by length (see WordDealer); if a theme is short on a length, the nearest are used.
